{{also|Luster}}
==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[lustre]] (UK/Commonwealth)

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-luster.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ʌstə(r)}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|lustre||lang=frm}}, from Old Italian [[lustro]], from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|lustro|lustrare|to brighten}}, akin to {{term|lux||lang=la|light}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{US}} [[shine|Shine]], [[polish]] or [[sparkle]].
#: ''He polished the brass doorknob to a high '''luster'''.
# By extension, [[brilliance]], [[attractiveness]] or [[splendor]].
#: ''After so many years in the same field, the job had lost its '''luster'''.
# [[refinement|Refinement]], polish or [[quality]].
#: ''He spoke with all the '''lustre''' a seasoned enthusiast should have.

=====Antonyms=====
* [[dullness]]
* [[lackluster]]

